# BIM Project Management

This repo is an internal web application for managing BIM projects, personnel, work, legal documents, finance, assets, and executive reporting. It is not an Electron or Autodesk Forma copy application.

## Product scope

- Core domains: projects, categories, tasks/subtasks, timesheets, leave, legal documents, payments/revenues/costs, assets, weekly plans/reports, checklists, meeting minutes, notifications, and executive dashboards.
- Roles: `system_admin`, `project_admin`, `project_leader`, and `member`; access must also be scoped to project membership.
- Financial and approval data require server-side authorization, validated state transitions, and auditability.

## Architecture

- Backend: TypeScript, Hono, Cloudflare Pages/Workers, D1/SQLite.
- Frontend: static SPA in `public/index.html` and `public/static/app.js`; `executive-dashboard.js` is loaded separately.
- Authentication: Bearer token through `Authorization`; never rely on client-side role checks.
- Database changes must be additive D1 migrations; do not use HTTP routes to initialize production schema.

## Repo map

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/index.tsx` | Hono API, middleware, and backend business logic |
| `src/renderer.tsx` | Hono HTML renderer |
| `public/index.html` | SPA markup and inline styles |
| `public/static/app.js` | Main frontend behavior and API client |
| `public/static/executive-dashboard.js` | Executive dashboard frontend |
| `migrations/*.sql` | Ordered D1 schema and seed migrations |
| `.cursor/**` | Rules and agent support files |

## Boundaries

- Do not add business logic only in the browser; calculations for money, VAT, fees, progress, and approval status belong in the backend.
- Every project-owned resource must enforce project access on list, detail, create, update, and delete routes.
- Every approval flow must enforce allowed transitions and record actor, time, old value, and new value.
- Reuse centralized authorization helpers; do not scatter new ad-hoc role checks.
- Preserve existing behavior with tests before splitting large monolithic files; refactor one business domain at a time.
- Do not edit dead forks such as `public/static/app.v2.js` or `style.v2.css`; production loads `app.js` and `executive-dashboard.js`.
- Never hardcode secrets or store credentials/tokens in logs, fixtures, or committed files.
- Never commit files >100 MiB or embed large base64 blobs in markdown.

## Language

- Product copy and internal documentation: Vietnamese; code and identifiers: English.
- Commits: conventional (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, …) imperative subject.
